                <pb facs="0357" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg245"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador O’Brien to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-01-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. O’Brien states that he has learned indirectly from the prime minister that
                    Japan will decline suggestion of December 18. He adds that a formal reply is
                    being considered, but is not yet ready.</p>
            </div>
